{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex. Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath()"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hamiltonianPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Path","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Path"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","te